# Local Go artifacts, mirroring agent/.gitignore (#333). A stray `go mod vendor` puts
# thousands of files into the build context and, worse, makes a build LOOK hermetic while
# the explicit GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly still resolves everything from the proxy. A crashed
# `go test ./internal/process` leaves multi-megabyte core dumps behind the same way. Both
# only cost cache invalidation and build time, but neither belongs in a build context.
#
# `core.*` alone would match only the context ROOT: .dockerignore patterns are anchored,
# so the very dumps named above -- which land in agent/internal/process/ next to the test
# that crashed -- would still be copied in. `**/core.*` is what actually excludes them.
agent/vendor/
core.*
**/core.*

# The image's own test scripts run from the checkout, never from inside the image.
test/